From: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0026] sensorhub/ssp: phase-1 raw-SSI boot-ROM sync before WHOAMI

The BCM47752 boot ROM only leaves its autobaud window after a raw SSI
autobaud+GetVersion ping driven over direct bcm_spi_sync()/bcm_ssi_rx() —
NOT the hello-gated /dev/ttyBCM circ-buffer that bcm_rxtx_work_func() drives
after bcm477x_hello() waits for mcu_resp.

bcm477x_rpc_get_version() already implements that phase-1 sequence in
bcm_gps_regs.c but has no caller in the native path.  Wire it into
nuxel_ssp_bringup_hw()'s rail cold-cycle recovery: after regulator_force_disable
+ regulator_enable re-enters the cold power-on window, run the raw-SSI sync so
the ROM transitions out of autobaud before initialize_mcu() issues WHOAMI.

This is one step of the two-phase download; the phase-2 reliable MemoryWrite/
StartScratchApp/ServiceStart/GetVersion records remain in the userspace native
downloader, which now runs after the ROM is actually in its download state.

NOTE: applies on top of 0023 (which supersedes 0020 for ssp_dev.c/ssp_sysfs.c)
and 0025.

Signed-off-by: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>

diff --git a/drivers/sensorhub/brcm/ssp_bbd.c b/drivers/sensorhub/brcm/ssp_bbd.c
index 3b949c8..0207994 100644
--- a/drivers/sensorhub/brcm/ssp_bbd.c
+++ b/drivers/sensorhub/brcm/ssp_bbd.c
@@ -14,6 +14,13 @@
  */
 
 #include "ssp.h"
+/* Forward declarations for the bbdpl direct-SSI boot-ROM path (no header
+ * include: bcm_gps_spi.h needs struct spi_device / circ_buf which ssp.h does
+ * not pull in).  Both symbols are built into the same vmlinux (CONFIG_BCM_GPS_
+ * SPI_DRIVER=y, CONFIG_SENSORS_SSP_BBD=y). */
+struct bcm_spi_priv;
+struct bcm_spi_priv *bcm_get_bcm_gps(void);
+int bcm477x_rpc_get_version(void *prv, char *id);
 
 
 bool ssp_dbg;
@@ -82,6 +89,32 @@ void nuxel_ssp_register_data(struct ssp_data *data)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(nuxel_ssp_register_data);
 
+/*
+ * Nuxel PWNAGE-SSP: phase-1 boot-ROM synchronisation.
+ *
+ * The BCM47752 boot ROM only enters its reliable-download state after a raw
+ * SSI autobaud+GetVersion ping.  The vendor kernel already implements this in
+ * bcm477x_rpc_get_version() (drivers/sensorhub/brcm/bbdpl/bcm_gps_regs.c),
+ * which drives bcm_spi_sync()/bcm_ssi_rx() DIRECTLY — it does NOT go through
+ * the hello-gated /dev/ttyBCM circ-buffer — and is exported but has no caller
+ * in the native path.  Call it here as the phase-1 handshake, after the rail
+ * has been genuinely cold-cycled, before any WHOAMI/reliable RPC.
+ *
+ * Returns 0 on a ROM reply, -ENODEV when the SPI transport is not up,
+ * -ETIMEDOUT when the ROM stays silent (the honest "not in cold window" case).
+ */
+static int nuxel_ssp_dl_romsync(void)
+{
+	struct bcm_spi_priv *priv = bcm_get_bcm_gps();
+
+	if (!priv)
+		return -ENODEV;
+	/* bcm477x_rpc_get_version() is the raw-SSI autobaud+GetVersion path. */
+	if (bcm477x_rpc_get_version(priv, "nuxel-dl"))
+		return -EIO;
+	return 0;
+}
+
 /*
  * Bring the sensor hub out of the post-probe shutdown state without the
  * Android vendor lhd daemon.  This performs only the kernel's own documented
@@ -161,6 +194,19 @@ int nuxel_ssp_bringup_hw(void)
 			ret, regulator_is_enabled(data->regulator_vdd_mcu_1p8));
 		msleep(300);	/* MCU boot time after rail settle */
 
+		/*
+		 * The hub is now in a genuine cold power-on window.  Drive the
+		 * phase-1 raw-SSI ROM sync (autobaud + GetVersion) so the boot ROM
+		 * transitions out of autobaud and can accept the firmware download
+		 * and the subsequent WHOAMI handshake.  bcm477x_rpc_get_version()
+		 * bypasses the hello-gated /dev/ttyBCM path and uses direct
+		 * bcm_spi_sync()/bcm_ssi_rx().
+		 */
+		{
+			int rsync = nuxel_ssp_dl_romsync();
+			pr_info("[SSPBBD] Nuxel bring-up: phase-1 ROM sync -> %d\n", rsync);
+		}
+
 		clean_pending_list(data);
 		data->resetting = false;
 		if (data->bSspShutdown)
